{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-139233e2-2dd4-4bdf-a6de-279bfe57ec8e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-942ffa3368047ddb","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9018-0anxspqq/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9018-E002.md","content":"# Per-project GPU-hour consumption reports with stable API and CSV export\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the administrator-facing chargeback reporting core: computation of per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges from the metering data delivered by the GPU usage metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990), a stable API for retrieving those reports, and CSV export of the same reports for finance tooling. It consumes metering data — it must not re-implement collection. Reports are denominated in GPU-hours; currency/cost-rate modelling is out of scope.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Compute per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over administrator-selectable time ranges, sourced from the metering data delivered by the GPU usage metering strategy, in accordance with the agreed metering data consumption contract.\n- Expose report retrieval via a stable API suitable for finance tooling integration.\n- Provide CSV export of the reports.\n- Keep the report computation consistent with the agreed consumption contract, applying the documented fallback adaptation if the metering data schema shifts.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given metering data is available per the agreed consumption contract, an administrator can retrieve a per-project GPU-hour consumption report for a selectable time range, and the reported values are correct against the underlying metering data.\n- The report retrieval API is stable, documented, and usable by finance tooling to retrieve the same reports.\n- Reports can be exported as CSV with the same values as the API returns.\n- The report computation consumes metering data only — no metering collection is re-implemented in this epic's deliverable.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)**: Administrators can view per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges, computed from the metering data delivered by RHAISTRAT-9990.\n- **HLR-2 (P1)**: Reports can be exported as CSV and retrieved via a stable API for finance tooling. Bundled with HLR-1 rather than split: the CSV export and the stable API are export modes of the same report surface over the same metering data — a separate epic would build the same data structure and API endpoint twice.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- External timing risk: the metering data becomes available only when the GPU usage metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990) lands. That availability is a schedule precondition owned outside this strategy; the acceptance criteria above are written on this epic's deliverable (correct reports once data is available per the agreed contract), not on the external landing date.\n- The metering data schema is not final until the metering strategy lands; this epic builds against the agreed consumption contract and its documented fallback.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":31739,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ab43a0e5f0ec23d","agent_id":"a5db3396ff8040630","session_id":"664fa4a8-d231-49b0-afe7-236ef7303dfd","uuid":"1f5cc6a8-73a5-4b2c-a23b-6c3b080ca745","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:11:11.094Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018"}
