{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-b0bb622e-e0ef-4588-912d-b166afecda51","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-92dc47049f613890","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9018-0anxspqq/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9018-E003.md","content":"# Dashboard admin view of current-month GPU consumption against Kueue quota\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the administrator-facing view in the RHOAI Dashboard that shows each project's current-month GPU consumption alongside that project's Kueue quota, so platform administrators can see who is consuming shared GPU capacity relative to their allocation. It presents data computed by the GPU chargeback reporting capability; it does not compute reports itself.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add an administrator-facing view to the Dashboard showing current-month per-project GPU-hour consumption against each project's Kueue quota.\n- Surface the view in the Dashboard's navigation for platform administrators, consistent with existing Dashboard integration patterns and admin-scoped access.\n- Consume the per-project GPU-hour report data produced by the chargeback reporting capability over the consumption surface agreed for the Dashboard (the Dashboard's standard integration interfaces govern this choice; the exact surface is an implementation decision for the Dashboard team).\n- Scope is presentation only: quota values come from the platform's existing Kueue quota model, consumption values from the chargeback reporting capability.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A platform administrator can open the Dashboard view and see current-month GPU consumption for each project alongside that project's Kueue quota.\n- The consumption values shown match the per-project GPU-hour reports computed by the chargeback reporting capability for the current month.\n- The view is not accessible to non-administrator users.\n- No report computation or metering data handling is implemented in the Dashboard — the view presents data from the chargeback reporting capability only.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-3 (P1)**: The Dashboard admin view shows current-month consumption against each project's Kueue quota.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Interface decision: the Dashboard historically integrates with component backends through the Kubernetes API and owns no data plane, while the chargeback reporting capability exposes a stable API for finance tooling. Whether this view consumes that API or a Kubernetes surface is an implementation decision for the Dashboard team; either way the epic builds against the report data contract, which is why it starts only after the reporting capability is defined.\n- Availability of consumption data depends on the metering data delivered by the GPU usage metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990); this is a schedule precondition external to this epic.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32477,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ab43a0e5f0ec23d","agent_id":"a5db3396ff8040630","session_id":"664fa4a8-d231-49b0-afe7-236ef7303dfd","uuid":"78fe3837-bb7a-46dc-97b2-579a09320c89","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:11:21.037Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018"}
