{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-93a3d61d-6d52-47aa-bba3-58cc51f42259","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a098f06b62d86650","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9018-0anxspqq/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9018-E004.md","content":"# Documentation for GPU chargeback report semantics and export integration\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic authors the administrator- and integrator-facing documentation for GPU chargeback reporting: what the reports mean (in particular, what counts as a GPU-hour), how to read the per-project consumption reports and the Dashboard view, and how finance tooling integrates with the report export. It is a Red Hat docs content process epic — substantive content authoring, not incidental touch-ups falling out of the code changes.\n\n## Scope\n\nContent outline:\n\n- **Report semantics**: what counts as a GPU-hour in the chargeback reports; how per-project consumption is attributed; what time ranges mean and how to select them; relationship between reported consumption and Kueue quota as shown in the Dashboard admin view.\n- **Reading the reports**: using the per-project GPU-hour consumption reports as a platform administrator, including the current-month Dashboard view.\n- **Export integration**: retrieving reports via the stable API and CSV export, aimed at finance tooling integrators.\n- Explicitly out of scope: currency/cost-rate modelling (reports are in GPU-hours, not dollars) and the metering collection pipeline itself.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Published documentation covers report semantics, including a clear definition of what counts as a GPU-hour, consistent with the implemented reporting behavior.\n- Published documentation covers export integration (stable API and CSV) sufficient for a finance tooling integrator to retrieve reports.\n- The content is technically reviewed against the implemented chargeback reporting capability and Dashboard view, with review sign-off recorded, before publication.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-4 (P2)**: Documentation covers report semantics (what counts as a GPU-hour) and export integration.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Team assignment is an assumption: the strategy contains no Impacted Teams table, so this epic is assigned to the docs team; verify the owning team before scheduling.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":33128,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ab43a0e5f0ec23d","agent_id":"a5db3396ff8040630","session_id":"664fa4a8-d231-49b0-afe7-236ef7303dfd","uuid":"1e003e7b-1d8f-42ec-b38b-cc474165bcea","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:11:30.140Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018"}
