{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5a6eb98cb7a590d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E002\n3\ttitle: Per-project GPU-hour consumption reports with stable API and CSV export\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9018-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9018-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the metering data schema shifts or the agreed consumption\n15\t    contract cannot be validated, rewrite the report computation's data-consumption\n16\t    approach against the revised schema before implementing the export surfaces.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: -1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: -1\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: Low\n30\tai_implementability_score: -1\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Per-project GPU-hour consumption reports with stable API and CSV export\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tThis epic delivers the administrator-facing chargeback reporting core: computation of per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges from the metering data delivered by the GPU usage metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990), a stable API for retrieving those reports, and CSV export of the same reports for finance tooling. It consumes metering data — it must not re-implement collection. Reports are denominated in GPU-hours; currency/cost-rate modelling is out of scope.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Compute per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over administrator-selectable time ranges, sourced from the metering data delivered by the GPU usage metering strategy, in accordance with the agreed metering data consumption contract.\n43\t- Expose report retrieval via a stable API suitable for finance tooling integration.\n44\t- Provide CSV export of the reports.\n45\t- Keep the report computation consistent with the agreed consumption contract, applying the documented fallback adaptation if the metering data schema shifts.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- Given metering data is available per the agreed consumption contract, an administrator can retrieve a per-project GPU-hour consumption report for a selectable time range, and the reported values are correct against the underlying metering data.\n50\t- The report retrieval API is stable, documented, and usable by finance tooling to retrieve the same reports.\n51\t- Reports can be exported as CSV with the same values as the API returns.\n52\t- The report computation consumes metering data only — no metering collection is re-implemented in this epic's deliverable.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- **HLR-1 (P0)**: Administrators can view per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges, computed from the metering data delivered by RHAISTRAT-9990.\n57\t- **HLR-2 (P1)**: Reports can be exported as CSV and retrieved via a stable API for finance tooling. Bundled with HLR-1 rather than split: the CSV export and the stable API are export modes of the same report surface over the same metering data — a separate epic would build the same data structure and API endpoint twice.\n58\t\n59\t## Risks / Notes\n60\t\n61\t- External timing risk: the metering data becomes available only when the GPU usage metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990) lands. That availability is a schedule precondition owned outside this strategy; the acceptance criteria above are written on this epic's deliverable (correct reports once data is available per the agreed contract), not on the external landing date.\n62\t- The metering data schema is not final until the metering strategy lands; this epic builds against the agreed consumption contract and its documented fallback.\n63\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b618458192a174a8","agent_id":"a19f88a96eed9a9ac","session_id":"664fa4a8-d231-49b0-afe7-236ef7303dfd","uuid":"bc42c27a-a939-4baa-b002-6b1c0e06fb68","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:13:19.566Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5a6eb98cb7a590d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9018 decomposition"}
