integration**: retrieving reports via the stable API and CSV export, aimed at finance tooling integrators.\n44\t- Explicitly out of scope: currency/cost-rate modelling (reports are in GPU-hours, not dollars) and the metering collection pipeline itself.\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t- Published documentation covers report semantics, including a clear definition of what counts as a GPU-hour, consistent with the implemented reporting behavior.\n49\t- Published documentation covers export integration (stable API and CSV) sufficient for a finance tooling integrator to retrieve reports.\n50\t- The content is technically reviewed against the implemented chargeback reporting capability and Dashboard view, with review sign-off recorded, before publication.\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- **HLR-4 (P2)**: Documentation covers report semantics (what counts as a GPU-hour) and export integration.\n55\t\n56\t## Risks / Notes\n57\t\n58\t- Team assignment is an assumption: the strategy contains no Impacted Teams table, so this epic is assigned to the docs team; verify the owning team before scheduling.\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b618458192a174a8","agent_id":"a19f88a96eed9a9ac","session_id":"664fa4a8-d231-49b0-afe7-236ef7303dfd","uuid":"6d5e36b0-4a0f-40aa-93cc-e08426850aaf","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:13:20.998Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-82099ee4d2785809","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9018 decomposition"}
